#N canvas 0 0 760 700 10;
#X text 12 8 opl3~ - raw-register + voice YMF262 (OPL3 \, the Sound Blaster 16 FM chip) on the Nuked-OPL3 core;
#X text 12 28 RAW LAYER: `reg <reg> <data>` with reg 0..0x1ff (bank 1 = 0x100|addr \, exactly the VGM port 0/1 bytes)\; `opl` is an alias so [vgm~]'s outlet-1 stream wires straight in\; a raw write implies raw mode (gates/velocity pin open \, the registers own the level)\; `reset` clears the chip. Register map: 0x20+n AM/VIB/EGT/KSR/MULT \, 0x40+n KSL/TL \, 0x60+n AR/DR \, 0x80+n SL/RR \, 0xE0+n waveform (carrier = +3 offsets from its modulator \, see ad_slot in the core)\; 0xA0+i FNUM low \, 0xB0+i keyon/blk/FNUM-hi \, 0xBD rhythm \, 0xC0+i feedback/CON/L-R \, 0x104 4-op masks \, 0x105 OPL3 mode;
#X text 12 130 VOICE LAYER (like ym2612~ \, one voice per chip channel \, bare = ch1 \, `chN ...` = channel N of 1..18): a message is a COMMAND STREAM - every word is a command with its own args \, so `gm 1 note 60 100` = load preset 1 AND play \, no comma needed (comma boxes `a \, b` still work). `chN` at the start scopes the whole message to channel N: `ch3 gm 1 note 62 100` = preset + note ON CH3 - it does NOT switch the sound over (no other channel is keyed off \, the gate inlet stays ch1). Commands: `note <midi> [vel]` (vel 0 = release) \, gate (inlet 2 = ch1's gate\; `chN gate 0` releases channel N) \, `alg <0-1>` (0 FM / 1 AM\; 4-op pairs: bits 0/1 = addressed/pair channel) \, `fb <0-7>` \, `pan <0-3>` (0 off / 1 L / 2 R / 3 both) \, `op <1-2> <param> <v>` (1 = carrier \, 2 = modulator\; params mul am vib egt ksr tl ksl ar dr sl rr ws) \, `gm <1-128>` (Mobilnik-v2 GM bank built in\; `bank <file.wopl>` loads others \, `bank default` restores);
#X text 12 210 OUTLETS (all signal): 0 = LEFT sum \, 1 = RIGHT sum (the chip's own stereo mix - each channel's 0xC0 pan bits) \, 2..19 = channels 1..18 alone (pan-independent\; a 4-op pair's second channel reads 0 - its operators sound in the first channel's outlet). WIRE BOTH SUMS: logs place whole phrases left-only or right-only \, and ONE multiplier fed by both outlets multiplies left BY right (an early shipped example did exactly that - pan-split notes vanished). mono 1 = both sums carry everything;
#X text 12 310 level: a full-scale carrier peaks at 1.0\; dense 18-channel mixes reach ~8 over +-1 - the final gain owns the headroom. OPL3 logs: [vgm~] outlet 1 -> [opl3~] (see the opl3-player example);
#X text 20 360 a 440 Hz tone on chip channel 1 (raw registers):;
#X msg 20 390 reset \, reg 261 1 \, reg 35 33 \, reg 67 0 \, reg 99 240 \, reg 131 8 \, reg 192 49 \, reg 160 68 \, reg 176 50;
#X text 20 440 the same tone through the voice layer \, then GM preset 1 \, then the same on chip channel 3:;
#X msg 20 470 reset \, note 69 100;
#X msg 20 500 note 0;
#X msg 160 500 gm 1 note 60 90;
#X msg 300 500 ch3 gm 1 note 62 90;
#X msg 440 500 ch3 gate 0;
#X obj 20 550 opl3~;
#X obj 20 600 *~ 0.3;
#X obj 140 600 *~ 0.3;
#X obj 20 650 dac~;
#X text 20 880 glide/slide (portamento);
#X msg 20 910 glide 80;
#X text 160 910 arm portamento 80 ms \, then notes sweep;
#X msg 20 940 note 60 100;
#X msg 20 970 note 72 100;
#X msg 20 1000 glide 0;
#X text 160 1000 off again;
#X msg 20 1030 slide 79 250;
#X text 160 1030 sweep to the pitch \, no key event;
